{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789316014,"nonce":"1vC2ot/xlyozr+UYEjXJ15HNi5I=","title":"Python: unannotated parameters typed from their call sites","message":"An unannotated parameter was `Object`, so a function written without annotations ran every operation on it through dynamic dispatch. The nbody port without annotations (`def advance(bodies, n, dt)`, `def __init__(self, x, y, ...)`) ran 15x slower than the same program annotated: boxed floats in every field, `zb_any_arith` on every operation, `py$getattr$x` on every field read.\n\nNow, for a function every call of which is in view (`types::closed_items`: a module function never mentioned but as a callee, never decorated, never rebound; a constructor never reached through `.__init__` on anything but `super()`, and not one of the exception classes the library and the lowering construct by name), an unannotated parameter's type is the join of what every call passes to it and what the body assigns to it. Calls are found by `types::Calls` over every body and the entry, with keyword arguments by name and left-out parameters taking their defaults; a call the parameters cannot be matched to, and any call from a nested function, lambda or comprehension (whose variables the walk does not type), passes `Object`. Exact where the program is consistent, dynamic where it is not: `twice(3); twice(2.5)` leaves `x` dynamic, `Point(3, 4); Plain(2, 5)` makes `y` an `i64`.\n\nThe module-wide fixed point no longer settles undecided values as dynamic between rounds (`infer_locals_open`): a local assigned from a function not yet typed stayed `Object` for good once it reached a monotone join (a field, a global, now a parameter). Only the end of inference settles. The entry body's own assignments are retyped every round too, so a module-level `total = compute(4)` is an `i64`; before, it was typed once before any function was.\n\nMethods other than `__init__` are not inferred: the override dispatcher needs one signature across a hierarchy, and a dynamic receiver can call any of them.\n\nConformance: `conformance/inference/` (parameters from call sites, reassigned parameters, functions as values, constructors including inherited and `super().__init__`, recursion and module-level globals).\n\nnbody without annotations: 10M steps in about 0.9 s, the same as annotated (was 22 s). The remaining gap to the ZynML `@reference` port (0.57 s) is Python's own semantics on the hot path: the bounds check with negative-index normalisation on each `bodies[j]`, the domain check in `math.sqrt`, and the pending-exception load and branch after each; the ZynML array index is unchecked.","files":null}]}